# +Intended, +Value, +Outcome, -Verdict, -Spent
# THE INTENDED ANSWERS OF THE CONTEST CORPUS (`contest.pl`), as data, and
# the limits every point is read under.
#
# `intended(Point, Outcome, Value)`: Outcome is a constructor of
# schema/outcome, `head` or `failed` (the program has no weak head); Value
# is a constructor of
# schema/intended_value, `boolean true`, `boolean false` (the Church
# Booleans of corpora/library/prelude/boolean), `natural Count`, or `none`
# when Outcome is `failed`. Each is the
# program's intended answer, argued in the comment above the point in
# `contest_clauses.pl`.
#
# `point_limits(Point, limits(Seconds, StackMegabytes, TableMegabytes))`:
# one second, 32 MB of stack and 32 MB of table space unless the point
# has raised limits below, each with the reason at the fact. Every setting
# reads a point under the same limits.
#   certificate(?Name, ?Term): multifile, a CERTIFICATE a corpus names, a
#   closed de Bruijn lambda term with one weak head (MIXINv8's
#   certificates); read by verdict/5.

#   ---- 1. linked list cycle ----
#
# The outcome is a constructor of schema/outcome, the value a constructor
# of schema/intended_value, a Boolean a Church Boolean of
# corpora/library/prelude/boolean. Each other text is from_cbor
# of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from
# corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an integer
# literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
